{"text": "Eichelberger Orthopedic Evaluations, PLLC\n1200 Hardy Street, Suite 2B, Hattiesburg, Mississippi 39401 · Tel. 601-555-0125 ·\nFax 601-555-0126\n\nINDEPENDENT MEDICAL EXAMINATION\n Examinee: Jacinta Olmedo-Varela · Date of birth: 07/22/1976 · Last four of SSN:\n5625\n Date of examination: November 4, 2025 · Date of injury: January 16, 2025\n Employer: Pascagoula Shipfitters, Inc. · Carrier: Bulwark Casualty Insurance ·\nClaim no. BCI-LS-2025-004418\n Requested by: Reginald Fauntleroy, claims examiner,\nrfauntleroy@bulwarkcasualty.example\n Interpreter: none needed. The examinee was told that no doctor-patient\nrelationship exists and that this report goes to the carrier.\n\nHistory given by the examinee\nMs. Olmedo-Varela is a 49-year-old pipefitter. She states that on January 16 she\nwas pulling a chain fall in a ship's engine room when she felt a \"pop\" in her low\nback. She finished the shift, reported it the next morning and was seen at the yard\nclinic. She has not worked since February 3. She describes constant low back pain\nradiating down the left leg to the foot, with numbness in the great toe. She rates it\n7 out of 10.\n\nShe denies any earlier back injury. When I asked specifically about 2018, she\nagreed that she had a lumbar microdiscectomy at L5-S1 in 2018 after a car\naccident, and said she \"did not think that counted because it was the other side.\"\n\nRecords reviewed\n Singing River Spine & Pain, Dr. Thuy-Vi Lam, notes of 2/11/25 through 10/02/25;\nchart no. SR-118204. Three epidural steroid injections (March, May and\nAugust).\n MRI lumbar spine, 02/20/2025: left paracentral disc extrusion at L4-L5\ncontacting the L5 nerve root; post-surgical change at L5-S1.\n Pharmacy printout: hydrocodone 10/325 four times daily since March,\ngabapentin 600 mg three times daily, duloxetine 60 mg.\n Form LS-1 authorizations and the employer's accident report.\n\nExamination\nHeight 5 ft 4 in, weight 171 lb. Gait antalgic on the left. Lumbar flexion limited to\n40 degrees with pain. Straight leg raise positive on the left at 35 degrees, negative\non the right. Weakness of left great-toe extension (4/5) and reduced sensation over\nthe dorsum of the left foot. Reflexes symmetric. Waddell signs: 1 of 5.\n\nShe became tearful when discussing work. She volunteered that she has been\ntreated for depression since her divorce and that she has been in recovery from\nalcohol for four years. I note this because of the current opioid dose.\n\nOpinions\n 1. Diagnosis: left L5 radiculopathy due to L4-L5 disc extrusion. The findings are\nconsistent with the mechanism described and are at a different level and side\nfrom the 2018 surgery.\n 2. Causation: more likely than not related to the January 16 work incident.\n 3. Maximum medical improvement: not reached. A surgical consultation is\nreasonable under 33 U.S.C. § 907.\n 4. Work status: sedentary duty only; no lifting over 10 lb.\n 5. If no surgery is performed, impairment under the AMA Guides, Sixth Edition\nwould be 12% of the whole person.\n 6. I recommend that Dr. Lam taper the hydrocodone; the examinee has run out\nearly twice according to the pharmacy record.\n\nCertification\nI examined the examinee personally for 45 minutes. Fee for examination and\nreport (CPT 99456): $1,850.00; no-show fee, had it applied, $600.\n\nHarlan B. Eichelberger, M.D., Board-certified orthopedic surgeon · Mississippi\nlicense no. 18844 · NPI 1447182209\n\nDictated 11/04/2025; signed electronically 11/07/2025 · HBE:tm", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 558 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Jacinta Olmedo-Varela", "Reginald Fauntleroy", "Thuy-Vi Lam", "Harlan B. Eichelberger"], "companies": ["Eichelberger Orthopedic Evaluations, PLLC", "Pascagoula Shipfitters, Inc.", "Bulwark Casualty Insurance", "Singing River Spine & Pain", "Duloxetine"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Hattiesburg", "Mississippi"], "health": ["low back pain", "numbness in the great toe", "epidural stero